{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792404628,"nonce":"oUwkmn7FSrubys8YhGyi7QHEd9I=","message":"Completion list and signature help landed.\n\n**Completion list**\neditor.showCompletions(items, ?from) opens a list under the character at `from` (the caret's word start by default). Items are CodeCompletion {label, insert, detail, docs, kind, filter, sort, more}. What is typed from `from` to the caret narrows the list: prefix, then word starts, then letters in order. Up/Down/PageUp/PageDown/Home/End move, Enter/Tab choose, Escape closes, as does the caret leaving the word, a non-word character, or no match. A press on a row chooses it. The choice goes in through applyEdits as one undo step, with any `more` edits (an import at the top) in the same step. hideCompletions() and completionsOpen() are there too. The list takes keys before the app's onKey.\n\n**Signature help**\nCodeHint has an `emphasis` range, offsets into `signature`, drawn bold with a tint. showHint({from, to, signature, emphasis}, true) at the caret gives the parameter a call is at. A text change closes a hint, so the app shows it again on each change.\n\nBoth rendered in dark and light: tools/snapshot/scenes/CodeEditorCompletion.hx and CodeEditorHint.hx with HINT=signature.","files":null}]}